gaingels-lightmatter:greenhouse:52212850.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter is leading the revolution in AI data center infrastructure, enabling the next giant leaps in human progress. The company invented the world’s first 3D-stacked photonics engine, Passage™, capable of connecting thousands to millions of processors at the speed of light in extreme-scale data centers for the most advanced AI and HPC workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter raised $400 million in its Series D round, reaching a valuation of $4.4 billion. We will continue to accelerate the development of data center photonics and grow every department at Lightmatter!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about tackling complex challenges, making an impact, and being an expert in your craft, join our team of brilliant scientists, engineers, and accomplished industry leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter is (re)inventing the future of computing with light!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About this Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a small, highly technical writing team embedded in the Product org at Lightmatter. We own all customer-facing technical content for our hardware and software products — giving engineers and researchers at the leading edge of AI and high-performance computing everything they need to get up and running fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Technical Writer, you will be key in defining the voice and structure of Lightmatter&#39;s customer-facing content. Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical writing activities for critical customer-facing product content, including hardware and software documentation for silicon photonics products such as data sheets, user guides, API documentation, release notes, and product briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive content strategy, governance, and quality standards across all documentation outputs, ensuring technical accuracy and alignment with Lightmatter&#39;s innovative product vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate extensively with Engineering, Marketing, Supply Chain, and Sales Teams to seamlessly integrate documentation with product development and release cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and manage authoring and publishing pipelines utilizing a DITA XML-based structured authoring environment and Git-based repositories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain scalable information architecture, metadata frameworks, and content models to optimize content reuse and simplify complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate documentation systems with engineering and PM tools (e.g., connecting Jira tasks to documentation status, using GitBook to automate documentation updates, and so on).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain cascading style sheets (CSS) within documentation platforms (e.g., Oxygen XML) to adapt content for web and PDF outputs.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pioneer the use of AI tools within the documentation lifecycle to accelerate content generation and partner with IT to pilot and scale AI-enabled authoring workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) to extract highly complex solution details and transform them into clear, modular, and consumable documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional experience in semiconductor technical writing, including at least two years in a leadership capacity. Expertise in DITA XML, structured authoring, and Component Content Management System (CCMS) platforms, preferably with proficiency in Oxygen XML Editor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and maintaining custom plugins and enhancements such as DITA-OT, XSLT, and CSS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in publishing workflows and version control systems (such as Git).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to identify and implement productivity tools and automation (for example, customized review/approval workflows, dynamic asset libraries) for a scalable modern platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with generative AI tools and proven ability to define their practical application in documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, project management, and proven ability for cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with relevant documentation tools such as MS Office Suite, MS Visio, and Adobe Acrobat/Framemaker/Photoshop/Illustrator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to read and write code for documentation purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with silicon photonics, fiber optics, or laser products is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation. The base salary range for this role determined based on location, experience, educational background, and market data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range: total compensation goes beyond base salary, it also includes a new hire equity grant, annual performance-based equity, and other rewards that recognize your impact and contribution.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$161,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Health Care Plan (Medical, Dental &amp;amp; Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Savings Matching Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance (Basic, Voluntary &amp;amp; AD&amp;amp;D)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Time Off (Vacation, Sick &amp;amp; Public Holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Family Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short Term &amp;amp; Long Term Disability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training &amp;amp; Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, hybrid workplace model&lt;/li&gt;
